{"t": 1794108885.5160513, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f Regression found: this change causes a production reconciliation error.\n\nSentry issue: [LEDGER-WORKER-9A](https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/) \u2014 `ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit (expected 1100, got 1099)`, first seen in release `ledger-worker@2026.11.3`.\n\n`int(amount_minor * rate)` truncates instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit (e.g. `convert(109999, 0.01)` returns 1099 instead of 1100), which breaks reconciliation. Fixed in `worker/rates.py` by restoring rounding (`round(amount_minor * rate)`).", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
